Search and rejection summary
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across presidential transcripts, INAI and FGR-related coverage, Baker Hughes and Pío family-allegation reporting, fact-checking pieces on AMLO speeches, and broader press-freedom context. I kept 14 distinct URLs in the dossier, with the reused items covering the repeated anti-press / truthfulness pattern and the new items covering personal-finance disclosure, family-scrutiny responses, a correction after an incorrect state-funds procedure, and specific false or misleading 2022 claims. I rejected broader corruption indices, generic press-freedom summaries, and 2023-2025 fact checks unless they directly bore on a 2022 AMLO statement or a 2022 filed declaration. I also rejected items that only described Mexico's inherited corruption environment without a ruler-specific personal-nexus claim.

Remaining gaps
- I did not find a conclusive 2022 finding of personal enrichment, bribery, or hidden ownership directly attributable to AMLO himself.
- The strongest family-conflict episode, Baker Hughes/José Ramón, remained contested and did not produce an independent finding of self-dealing by AMLO.
- Evidence on appointments, loyalists, and transactional favoritism is thinner than the evidence on public truthfulness and media attacks.
- More search would help on 7B.3, 7B.4, 7B.5, and 7B.9, especially if you want stronger documentary proof on contracts, beneficial ownership, or appointment patterns tied to close associates.

